<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3673" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">armātus</span></b> , ūs,
			m.
		armo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>armor</i> (only in the abl.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">haud dispari,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					33, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cretico,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					42, 55 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">armatu sustinendo assueti milites,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Fronto, Prim. Hist. Fragm. 2, p.
				341</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Meton.</b>, <i>armed soldiers</i>
			(cf. armatura, I. B.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gravi armatu,</span>”
				<i>with the heavy-armed</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					37, 41</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">magnā parte impedimentorum
					relictā in Bruttiis, et omni graviori armatu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 26,
					5</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
